Tick-C 1.0 beta 9 modernization
================================

This work is based on Tick-C 1.0 beta 9, originally distributed by the MIT
Parallel and Distributed Operating Systems group, and on lcc by Christopher
W. Fraser and David R. Hanson.

The original Tick-C permission notice is preserved at:
  doc/modernization/phase0/upstream-license-notice.md

The complete lcc copyright and redistribution conditions are preserved at:
  doc/original-lcc/COPYRIGHT.lcc
  LICENSES/LicenseRef-LCC-1994.txt

The Tick-C distribution permission notice is preserved at:
  LICENSES/LicenseRef-TCC-1996.txt

Standalone modernization files identified in `REUSE.toml` are licensed under
the MIT License preserved at:
  LICENSES/MIT.txt

Modernization changes to historical files and architecture files derived from
historical implementations inherit the Tick-C and lcc conditions rather than
adding a separate MIT layer.

The `config/install-sh` fallback is taken from GNU Automake 1.18.1. Its
X Consortium permission notice and the public-domain status of later Free
Software Foundation changes are preserved in that file.

This modernization is maintained for research and instruction. Its approved
publication scope is free source distribution under the inherited Tick-C and
lcc conditions; sale, commercial permission, binaries, packages, CI artifacts,
and container images are not part of that approval.

Additional copyright and permission notices appear in individual files. See
LICENSE.md and doc/modernization/release/source-inventory.md before copying or
redistributing this repository.
